 5. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Anthem, Covenant's "heavy-payload, long-range cruise missile." Photo: Courtesy of Covenant

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 💥 Covenant emerged from stealth today, logging more than $250 million raised across three rounds. Backers include Andreessen Horowitz and Founders Fund. Advisers include former Deputy Defense Secretary Kathleen Hicks .

 Why it matters: The D.C.-based startup already completed a live-fire test of its Anthem cruise missile at the U.S. Army's Project Convergence . 💭 My thought bubble: Where it builds is notable. The U.S. Germany. Israel. 📊 The Pentagon's Chief Digital and Artificial Intelligence Office has turned to Red Cell Partners to pilot a shared-savings contracting framework. The arrangement is worth up to $100 million.

 Why it matters: "For nearly two years, we have worked alongside CDAO and the Navy to define how shared savings could eliminate inefficiencies via agentic AI," Red Cell founder Grant Verstandig wrote in a blog post . "Now it's time to execute." 💭 My thought bubble: A venture studio prime, with portfolio companies as subs? Interesting. 🇸🇦 The State Department approved the potential sale of Joint Direct Attack Munitions-Extended Range and AGT-1500 engines, used in M1 Abrams tanks, to Saudi Arabia .

 Why it matters: The deals are together valued at $5.75 billion. 💭 My thought bubble: Remember when the White House said Saudi Arabia wants to buy hundreds of American tanks? 🗳️ President Trump nominated Hung Cao to be the next Navy secretary. Trump on social media described him as a "true warrior."

 Why it matters: Cao is already in the role — in an acting capacity — following the sudden dismissal of John Phelan. 💭 My thought bubble: Riley Ceder at Military Times has a months-old rundown on Cao's priorities, including "alpha males and alpha females." 
 
